<title>CANADA: Ontario regulator adopts electronic disclosure.</title>
<headline>Ontario regulator adopts electronic disclosure.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ontario Securities Commission (OSC) adopted a ruling on Thursday that will provide for the implementation of the System for Electronic Document Analysis and Retrieval in the Canadian province of Ontario.</p>
<p>The securities regulator said in a statement that the rulng has been delivered to Ontario's Minister of Finance for approval under Ontario's Securities Act. &quot;Provided the rule becomes effective, domestic public companies and mutual funds will be required to commence filing certain disclosure materials electronically as of January 1, 1997,&quot; the OSC said.</p>
<p>	  -- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
